@*
    Activating a new account (Task 1 8.2). Accounts are created by the Managing
    Director, who hands over a temporary password; there is no self-registration
    and no activation email. The first sign-in opens "Set your password", and no
    other page opens until the user has chosen their own. This page explains the
    steps; it collects nothing.
*@
@{
    Layout = "_AuthLayout";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Activate your account";
}

<a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm auth-back" asp-action="Login">
    <svg class="ico ico-sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-left" /></svg> Back to sign in
</a>

<h1>Activate your account</h1>
<p class="lede">
    Your account is made by the Managing Director. You activate it by signing in once
    with the temporary password they give you, then choosing your own.
</p>

<ol class="auth-steps">
    <li>Get your temporary password from the Managing Director, in person.</li>
    <li>Sign in with your work email address and the temporary password.</li>
    <li>On <strong>Set your password</strong>, choose a password of at least 12 characters with an upper-case letter, a lower-case letter and a number.</li>
    <li>From then on, sign in with your own password.</li>
</ol>

<div class="notice notice-info" role="note">
    <svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-lock" /></svg>
    <div>
        <strong>There is no public sign-up.</strong>
        If you have not been given a temporary password, ask the Managing Director to create your account.
    </div>
</div>

<a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg btn-block auth-action" asp-action="Login">Sign in with your temporary password</a>
